# Anchored to the repo root on purpose: a bare `data/` also matches source
# packages named `data` at any depth (aaa/data/, aaa/api/routes/data/) and
# silently kept 57 tracked-by-intent files out of git.
/data/
*.db
*.sqlite3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Graphify (local knowledge graph, not committed by default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphify-out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporary / generated evidence
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tmp_evidence/
*.tmp
*.bak
# Runtime LLM audit trail. Append-only and unbounded — it reached 41 MB while
# tracked, most of the repo's git history. Regenerated on every run.
logs/audit/*.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pid
backups/qdrant_snapshots/

# repo-context (generated, local-first). No trailing slash: a worktree links
# `.context` to the main checkout's, and `.context/` matches only a directory.
.context
.claude/commands/context-update.md
.claude/commands/update-docs.md
logs/errors/*.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Thesis material and client documents
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The exposé and any literature it cites belong to the thesis, not to the
# codebase, and carry their own licensing.
data/Updated_Expose_S5_UAGF_TAM_AAA_Updated.txt
*_Expose_*.txt
*.bib
literature/
thesis/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only run records
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One place for everything that records what a particular run did: the per-call
# assessment transcripts, the defect-and-fix logs, the evidence kept from a run,
# and the per-run analysis that generates them. Official documentation lives in
# `docs/` and is tracked; this is the paper trail, it is large, it regenerates,
# and some of it describes a real provider's system. See local/README.md.
/local/

# Mariposa-Edu GmbH is a real provider. Their intake bundle is their own
# technical documentation, and the per-call transcript of an audit of it (now
# `local/assessments/run_2026-09-10/`) runs to 5 MB. Neither is ours to publish,
# and the repository does not need them: every test that reads them is
# `skipif`-guarded, and `aaa.tools.run_preflight` reports a clear error when the
# case document it is pointed at is absent. Keep them locally; not distributed.
mock/06_mariposa_edu_gmbh/
scripts/fixtures/cgsa/mariposa-*.json
data/Mariposa/

# Driver output: screenshots the wizard driver takes and files the dashboard's
# download buttons save. Both are per-run artefacts, not source.
screenshots/
downloads/

# The two bundles `python bootstrap.py` unpacks — the Mariposa intake bundle
# and the regulatory corpus — are handed over separately, never committed.
/mariposa.zip
/corpus.zip
